#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:5
#: 28fd7007c8bc445b84a011dc6351dd5a
msgid "Plane Failsafe Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:7
#: 1e0059755b334800b97c844cfc429d67
msgid "Plane has a limited failsafe function which is designed to do four things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:10
#: 43ae19af56ea422d8b0aef82d41b8ae6
msgid "Detects a RC Failsafe condition and then initiating a defined response, such as returning to home. Detection of an RC Failsafe is either a complete loss, or corruption, of RC signals, or the receiver sets a FS bit in its data stream for those protocols supporting it (SBUS, etc.), or that the throttle channel PWM value falls below a certain point set by :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>`. This RC failsafe must be enabled by setting :ref:`THR_FAILSAFE<THR_FAILSAFE>` = 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:11
#: f8c9ee58a82f4f2dae007fcc8e48618a
msgid "Optionally, detect loss of telemetry (GCS Failsafe) and take an programmable action, such as switching to return to launch (RTL) mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:13
#: 1f523ba38d974183b2b35388b64cfde4
msgid "Either of the above have two phases: Short Failsafe which occurs a programmable time after loss of RC or telemetry, which allows optionally circling to try to recover the signals, and if the loss persists longer, a Long Failsafe which determines what long term action is to be taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:15
#: 192286e43fc549d4b1ee0b020cf41d15
msgid "Detect loss of GPS for more than 20 seconds and switch into Dead Reckoning mode until GPS signal is regained. See https://youtu.be/0VMx2u8MlUU for a demo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:16
#: 79bd92cff2234ec5ae4157a2c06c28f9
msgid "Optionally, detect low battery conditions (low voltage/remaining capacity) and initiate a programmable response, such as returning to home. ArduPilot supports this on multiple batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:18
#: 37854ea077fc48d0b5ccecaad3f54353
msgid "Here's what the failsafe **will not do**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:20
#: 5767221b087d4f8d8dabb19ce92ce44f
msgid "Detect if one or more individual RC channel has failed or become disconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:21
#: ae8fb7420f5c4f68ab17108fad4ed9cf
msgid "Detect if you're flying too far away or are about to hit the ground"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:22
#: aa5a39f042d845f58d6456eab790fcf2
msgid "Detect autopilot hardware failures, such as low-power brownouts or in-air reboots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:23
#: 0ca5349951ba4e1684fde0ad6016cd33
msgid "Detect if the Plane software is not operating correctly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:24
#: 5eacc4d2663043c384ed8994ef38448a
msgid "Detect other problems with the aircraft, such as motor failures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:25
#: 90edd31f7bf9436cadbb399064c19580
msgid "Otherwise stop you from making setup or flight mistakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:28
#: f9223ab24ce9480e82020d046cacb5e3
msgid "See :ref:`advanced-failsafe-configuration` for extended failsafe configurations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:32
#: 9fd845f809c541888d9e3e84b04979b3
msgid "RC Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:37
#: c9521f4d94294298aae241555a847f81
msgid "Radio Signal Failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:39
#: 0ffb25cab7c043a694ca4d60b7f8e785
msgid "If the received signal is lost or the control information corrupted for greater than :ref:`RC_FS_TIMEOUT<RC_FS_TIMEOUT>` (default = 1 sec), or the receiver sets its \"failsafe bit\" in protocols which have this (like Sbus, FPort, etc.), or RC_OVERRIDES are lost if :ref:`using a GCS only <common-gcs-only-operation>` is being used, then an RC Failsafe condition occurs and the actions described in the :ref:`RC Failsafe Actions<fs_actions>` section below will be taken, if the :ref:`THR_FAILSAFE<THR_FAILSAFE>` parameter is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:41
#: be831d9ffe9f424cad8ef3ae348042e3
msgid "by setting :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` bit 2, you can force ArduPilot to ignore the \"failsafe\" bits in the protocol, and only initiate RC Failsafe due to missing or corrupted control information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:44
#: b2e4681a7cee4105ba1e63b9e1fd587a
msgid "Throttle Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:46
#: 7ef4d6c4508d4a48a09bc140e84bc6b4
msgid "In addition, if the throttle signal falls below a threshold set by :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` and the :ref:`THR_FAILSAFE<THR_FAILSAFE>` is = 1, an RC Failsafe condition will be entered, a Ground Control Station text message (\"Throttle Failsafe On\") will be sent (to differentiate from a Radio Signal Failure Failsafe), and the actions described in the RC Failsafe Actions section below will be taken."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:49
#: 91f4669ad9e44d8c871b85e02410a7e6
msgid "Throttle Failsafe Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:51
#: 4c51d6984d564efdabfee62e2fa7f2b3
msgid "Throttle Failsafe is not required. If you wish to have failsafe protection against RC signal loss, but not setup a throttle signal controlled failsafe, then set :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` lower than the lowest RC throttle signal that can be sent to the autopilot from the receiver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:53
#: 34805ef4f9764e138f0adeb11538cbbe
msgid "In order to activate the Throttle Failsafe, the throttle signal received by the autopilot must be below :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>`. Once setup, this can be controlled by the pilot to initiate Throttle failsafe intentionally (for testing, or instead of setting up an RTL position on the flight mode switch), or by having the receiver, itself, send that value when it loses RC signal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:55
#: 9792478d14dd4385a6d0a87c1c7a2f1c
msgid "having the receiver send a pre-set failsafe throttle value upon signal loss is NOT recommended and can lead to issues if a battery level failsafe is setup in QuadPlanes. Setting the receiver to send \"no pulses\" is much preferred. However, some very old receivers will only send a low throttle level in failsafe, see the section below, :ref:`Old Receivers <old_RX>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:57
#: 60ba930c409e40a2b1e74910212dac62
msgid "The system must be setup such that the throttle channel's signal can go below :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` (Default is 950), but still be above it for normal low throttle stick operation. Before doing the :ref:`RC Calibration<common-radio-control-calibration>` setup step which determines normal operating ranges for the throttle channel and others, make sure that the low throttle stick position on your transmitter is above :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>`. This can be done several ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:59
#: f9bb241a2a98433ca61bfbd788b4bbbf
msgid "When you do the :ref:`RC Calibration <common-radio-control-calibration>` setup step, change the trim tab for the throttle channel to adjust its signal 40-50us above :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` at low throttle stick. This will be the normal operating position. Lowering the trim tab and setting the :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` to that value allows initiating a failsafe at low trim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:60
#: 7cbf1249896f4fb0ae356fe46b58ef26
msgid "Setup a transmitter switch that you will use to force failsafe such that it forces the throttle channel signal, using a mix, to below :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` when activated, allowing normal operation otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:65
#: f1c94677aebd4285af0aac80292e8638
msgid "RC Failsafe Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:67
#: de69758a616045759c2c32ec9fa2eba3
msgid "When RC Failsafe is entered, all RC inputs (except throttle in the case of Throttle Failsafe), are ignored as the autopilot takes its failsafe actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:68
#: f6e8366697d7445b892305a597f494a6
msgid "First, the autopilot will go into Short Failsafe when it detects RC Failsafe for more than 0.5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:69
#: 2e6280991fe3423ab830b0b38b8db247
msgid "A message will be displayed on your Ground Control Station(GCS), or OSD, if its message panel is enabled, that a Short Failsafe is active, and the autopilot will take the :ref:`FS_SHORT_ACTN<FS_SHORT_ACTN>`, if enabled.  The default is CIRCLE mode. This is intended to possibly allow the vehicle's changing orientation to re-acquire the signal, but other actions can be assigned. See :ref:`FS_SHORT_ACTN parameter below <failsafe-parameters>` for how each mode responds to the selected action value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:70
#: 1e73104fe65040de9f4fbbc112e7ca2d
msgid "If the condition causing the Short Failsafe is removed, the vehicle will return to the previous mode, and a message will be displayed that Short Failsafe is cleared. If it was a Throttle Failsafe that caused the RC Failsafe, and throttle was increased in order to exit, then an additional message will be sent stating that the Throttle Failsafe is OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:71
#: 43612fc5fb6749268574447ab6b1428e
msgid "If the condition causing the Short Failsafe persists longer than :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` seconds the autopilot will go into Long Failsafe, send a message to the GCS that it has been entered, and execute the :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` action, if enabled. The default setting for Long Failsafe action to take is RTL (Return to Launch). See :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN parameter below <failsafe-parameters>` for how each mode responds to the selected action value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:72
#: 02be598ef948409f82d4f0de358124b4
msgid "If the RC Failsafe condition is later exited, a message will be displayed that the Long Failsafe is cleared, but the flight mode will not revert. If it was a Throttle Failsafe that caused the RC Failsafe, and throttle was increased in order to exit, then an additional message will be sent stating that the Throttle Failsafe is OFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:74
#: 1bef52a42f8d4104817176603c1f490b
msgid "The action set by :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` will continue even if your RC signal is reacquired, if the flight mode is the same as it was before the failsafe action began. Once RC signal is reacquired, the :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` can be exited via a mode change on the :ref:`FLTMODE_CH<FLTMODE_CH>`. If the mode on the RC transmitter was changed during the failsafe period, then this changed mode is entered after the RC signal is restored. In addition, other failsafes, such as battery failsafe, can also change the mode, if they occur subsequently to the RC signal loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:77
#: be318295aab545e896dddd5383eeca97
msgid "Bench Testing RC Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:79
#: fb2b8025255f427ea89662a99ba33827
msgid "Power up the system and verify that you are seeing RC control in the Mission Planner SETUP->Mandatory Hardware->Radio Calibration tab and in a non-auto mode (Manual, Stabilize, FBW are ok). Check that normal throttle movements to idle do NOT trigger a failsafe and normal control stick movements are observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:80
#: 738e368310ad4befb4fd24c3b70cd6c5
msgid "Switch to Mission Planners DATA View tab. Turn off the transmitter. You should see the flight mode switch to :ref:`FS_SHORT_ACTN<FS_SHORT_ACTN>`. After :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` sec, if enabled, the flight mode should then switch to :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>`. Turn the transmitter back on and change flight modes. The Long Failsafe flight mode should change to the selected mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:81
#: 39f45cf809b346c7a1cf277e1822478b
msgid "If Throttle Failsafe is setup (ie via trim tab or transmitter switch). Check that it operates correctly by activating it and watching for Short and Long Failsafes to occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:83
#: e5a80cd196a044c4ad3be29f2a33002c
msgid "If you observe this behavior, your RC Failsafe function has been set up correctly. If not, recheck that the parameters above have been set correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:88
#: 5c664595d06d46a099b2eca312a415b4
msgid "Older Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:90
#: 1ef8dd4615b34a54a24770cf3b83289c
msgid "Some very old RC receivers cannot be set to send \"no pulses\" when losing RC signal and simple hold the ROLL/PITCH/YAW RC channels at their last value and set the throttle channel to its minimum PWM value (low throttle). For those, the only way to setup an RC failsafe is to set the :ref:`THR_FS_VALUE<THR_FS_VALUE>` to slightly above that value and use the transmitters trim tab to raise the idle stick value 40-50us above that for normal operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:92
#: a5c05baebeaa4cf58467986b35be17bc
msgid "be sure to do :ref:`ESC calibration<common-esc-calibration>` after you have setup the failsafes and throttle ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:94
#: 99ec86e340cc4f2ca5213ddb125dbebd
msgid "**Transmitter Tutorials:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:96
#: 3c94e1d34bd5402bb4d61dc00f37b09b
msgid "`Spektrum Setup <https://diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/spektrum-dx8-and-ar8000-failsafe-setup>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:100
#: f01a7e2be1f64b3e9d10fc1c38321c61
msgid "GCS Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:102
#: e1fc4675d68e4374ab799e720ca88265
msgid "**How it works.** When flying while using telemetry on the GCS, the autopilot can be programmed to trigger into failsafe mode if it loses telemetry from its primary GCS (set by :ref:`MAV_GCS_SYSID <MAV_GCS_SYSID>`). In the event that the autopilot stops receiving MAVlink (telemetry protocol) heartbeat messages from it, :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` applies just as in the case of a long Throttle Failsafe. See :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN parameter below <failsafe-parameters>` for how each mode responds to the selected action value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:107
#: de7e76847ea84948aacc37cb1f965269
msgid "**Setup.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:109
#: cb3483d919b04059a39b33ee877c6021
msgid "Set :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABL<FS_GCS_ENABL>` to 1 to enable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:110
#: 3548dd9166224538bcf37e147e97ac37
msgid "Connect to the Mission Planner via telemetry. Verify on the bottom right corner of the HUD that you are armed and “flying” in a non auto mode (Manual, Stabilize, FBW are ok). Be sure you have the GCS connected or failsafe will occur immediately, possibly starting the motors!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:113
#: 1006b83ddfc741f0bc2e3d11604d94ac
msgid "Unplug the telemetry radio getting telemetry from the primary GCS. After a few minutes power off your autopilot. (Remember the autopilot will not go fully into failsafe until :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` seconds of MAVLink inactivity have passed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:116
#: d3ef004d14344c088ef28a09df1a9aa5
msgid "Connect your autopilot to the mission planner and pull the logs. Verify on the log that the autopilot went into RTL after :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` sec of MAVLink inactivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:120
#: bc94a65a55c14ed3a066cda9accd8ea6
msgid "Configuring for Ground Control Station Control beyond RC range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:122
#: a6b775c2e76f40318941968f039d4c74
msgid "If the telemetry range exceeds the RC transmitter range, then it may be desired to prevent loss of RC signal from initiating a failsafe. Reliance on the above GCS failsafe would be then be used to provide failsafe protection. In order to prevent the RC system from interfering with GCS operation, set :ref:`THR_FAILSAFE<THR_FAILSAFE>` = 2. This prevents the RC failsafe action from being taken, but still detects the failsafe condition and ignores the RC inputs, preventing possible interference to Ground Control Station control of the vehicle. Control via the RC system can be resumed once back into its range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:125
#: 7f4e76a593954b1ab5cf5aff6b7758c3
msgid "Configuring for valid RC outputs while in RC Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:127
#: 6d792e15b7644ff78ac84c75981aed3c
msgid "Normally, the RC channels are ignored when in RC Failsafe (except the throttle channel, but for failsafe detection exit only). Sometimes it is desirable to allow the preset signal loss values( for receivers capable of this ), to be used in the event of an RC failsafe. For example, parachute activation, or other controls via RC passthrough (see :ref:`common-auxiliary-functions`) could be desired when in RC failsafe. For receivers with this capability and which use a FS data bit, setting :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` bit 2 to \"1\", can accomplish this. In this case, the FS bit is ignored. Upon RC signal loss the receiver would go to its pre-set channel outputs values, but a failsafe action would not be taken by ArduPilot, since the receiver is still outputting valid data as far as ArduPilot can detect. The fixed RC channel values would processed as normal by ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:130
#: 62acd193825141c0961d47612842193a
msgid "In this setup, it is usually necessary to make sure that the flight mode channel will force an RTL or AUTO mission to return the vehicle when the receiver loses RC signal, since no failsafe action will be taken, otherwise. The values of the flight control channels for Roll, Pitch, Yaw and Throttle need to be appropriately set also (usually neutral positions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:132
#: 5680f50243f8414b8e7485baf94bb6f5
msgid "Since the autopilot cannot know if the RC link is lost in this configuration, it is possible to get into dangerous situations, especially with QuadPlanes. For example, you are low on battery and far away, and the battery failsafe is active and attempting a VTOL land to prevent a crash. As it drops out of RC range, it will switch to the RC failsafe mode set in the receiver, and attempt to execute that, canceling the battery failsafe action, and ultimately resulting in a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:137
#: d3c4d9737e70499f94fe8e933847b4c0
msgid "Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:141
#: bfcdcb5419554b5eb2d32d30b0750e9e
msgid "This failsafe requires the vehicle have a working :ref:`Power Module <common-powermodule-landingpage>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:143
#: 24c77ebff3ee4c998167ba5bd547260f
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to 10 batteries/power monitors. All the  discussion below applies to those optional batteries also. Each can trigger a failsafe and each can have different actions and setup values. In addition, a group of batteries can be treated as a single unit, see ``BATTx_MONITOR`` = 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:145
#: 376b4fea7f434c3094060930a89ed4b7
msgid "the battery low failsafe voltage must be higher than the battery critical failsafe voltage or a pre-arm error will occur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:149
#: e9871b0855034800856afaddbdc99939
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:151
#: 823f4d2f2bd4447db4487c117e4d5d6e
msgid "If enabled and set-up correctly the battery failsafe will trigger if the main battery's"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:153
#: 690cb6de6cef4f8a827d1387459b6d7a
msgid "voltage drops below the voltage held in the :ref:`BATT_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` parameter (or FS_BATT_VOLTAGE in older versions) for more than 10 seconds. If set to zero (the Plane default value) the voltage based trigger will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:154
#: c475177b95c042c090e2feedfc2ccade
msgid "remaining capacity falls below the :ref:`BATT_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>` parameter (or FS_BATT_MAH in older versions) 20% of the battery's full capacity is a good choice (i.e. \"1000\" for a 5000mAh battery).  If set to zero the capacity based trigger will be disabled (i.e. only voltage will be used)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:157
#: 6069f5a8f2424e8f99aa6bfc601b3f64
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:159
#: a856cb8ea81c45979a8d41d6ddee2e7d
msgid "When the failsafe is triggered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:161
#: da9729479b754150aa8075977bf302bf
msgid "Buzzer will play a loud low-battery alarm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:162
#: 99aae927e31241258761e482db1161ea
msgid "LEDs will flash yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:163
#: 1016b29e553a4f148d8054f08f4e8936
msgid "A warning message will be displayed on the ground station's HUD (if telemetry is connected)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:164
#: 87ff4ea5182648b7a427a86ae295e54f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>`  will be executed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:167
#: 888bd88e5a554eafa233dcc428a1756e
msgid "Two-Stage Battery Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:169
#: 35010803d5f04b909bc2595b07f64984
msgid "Plane includes a two-layer battery failsafe.  This allows setting up a follow-up action if the battery voltage or remaining capacity falls below an even lower threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:171
#: 87a49ad365234ffeae0ee27d25825c4d
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` - holds the secondary (lower) voltage threshold.  Set to zero to disable. Default is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:172
#: 9e522cbcdb884585867e335439545b48
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>` - holds the secondary (lower) capacity threshold.  Set to zero to disable. Default is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:173
#: 1dae6a9dd23d41b9aace034350ea9534
msgid ":ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` - holds the secondary action to take.  A reasonable setup would be to have :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 1 (RTL) and :ref:`BATT_FS_CRT_ACT <BATT_FS_CRT_ACT>` = 2 (Land)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/apms-failsafe-function.rst:176
#: 275bfda4711e49c18f037e036f7f8029
msgid "Advanced Battery Failsafe Settings"
